    <main class="page-main">
        <section class="section two-col">
            <article class="surface-card">
                <h2>Our mission</h2>
                <p>
                    SLOSH develops practical, open, and community-centered water science. We work alongside local
                    partners to turn technical climate, stream, and infrastructure information into tools people can
                    use for planning and action.
                </p>
                <p>
                    Our projects span machine learning for flood awareness, climate data portals, wastewater planning,
                    and policy-grounded support for local governance.
                </p>
            </article>

            <aside class="surface-card">
                <h2>Focus areas</h2>
                <div class="pill-row">
                    <span class="pill">Flood Risk Intelligence</span>
                    <span class="pill">Climate Data Access</span>
                    <span class="pill">Water Quality & Infrastructure</span>
                    <span class="pill">GIS Decision Support</span>
                    <span class="pill">Community Partnerships</span>
                    <span class="pill">Open Reproducible Science</span>
                </div>
            </aside>
        </section>

        <section class="section">
            <h2>Current priorities</h2>
            <p class="section-subtitle">
                These themes guide our active collaborations across university, agency, and community partners.
            </p>
            <div class="grid grid-3">
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>American Samoa climate intelligence</h3>
                    <p>Building accessible dashboards and forecast tools to support adaptation planning.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>Wastewater and watershed planning</h3>
                    <p>Integrating environmental, social, and infrastructure data to prioritize investments.</p>
                </article>
                <article class="card">
                    <h3>AI for stream monitoring</h3>
                    <p>Using camera and sensor data to improve stream condition awareness in real time.</p>
                </article>
            </div>
        </section>
